<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="050" project="dotnet-10-upgrade-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>FR-15 — gather region/slot evidence (resolves the 2 execution-time unknowns)</title>
    <phase>P5 Non-prod cutover (OPERATOR-DRIVEN)</phase>
    <gate>042 complete</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>STANDARD</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Evidence-gathering + Azure read commands; operator-driven; no code change.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Run az read commands + record; well-specified.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>OPERATOR-DRIVEN — needs Azure credentials; gate for the non-prod cutover.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>042</deps>
    <tags>deployment, dotnet, migration</tags>
    <estimated-effort>1 hour</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>OPERATOR-DRIVEN. Gather the two execution-time verifications the spec deferred: (1) run `az webapp list-runtimes --os-type linux` for the prod subscription/region and confirm `DOTNETCORE:10.0` is available (CLI/ARM works even if the portal picker lags), and (2) confirm a dev/staging slot exists or can be created on the target App Service without disrupting current config. Record both as FR-15 evidence.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE release engineer + platform developer. Expert in Azure App Service runtimes, deployment slots, and az CLI. Follow ADRs strictly.</role>
  <goal>`notes/region-slot-evidence.md` contains the pasted `az webapp list-runtimes` output confirming `DOTNETCORE:10.0` in the prod region, and confirmation that a staging slot exists or a clean creation path is verified — resolving the two open Unresolved Questions in spec.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>spec Dependencies + Unresolved Questions: "Region runtime evidence" and "Slot availability" are execution-time verifications, not planning blockers. Design §7: colon form for `list-runtimes`. This is the first P5 task and a prerequisite to the non-prod deploy (051). It is operator-driven because it needs Azure credentials to the prod subscription.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="new">projects/dotnet-10-upgrade-r1/notes/region-slot-evidence.md</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">projects/dotnet-10-upgrade-r1/notes/slot-swap-runbook.md</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="042" status="pending">Runbook exists (defines the slot the evidence confirms).</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project">OPERATOR-DRIVEN: requires Azure credentials; do not fabricate output — paste real `az` results. If the runtime is not listed in-region, STOP (see escalation) rather than proceeding to deploy.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Read-only Azure commands only in this task — no config changes to the live App Service (slot creation, if needed, is verified as a path, executed with the operator).</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>Azure region runtime availability + slot verification</topic>
    <files>
      <file>projects/dotnet-10-upgrade-r1/spec.md</file>
      <file>projects/dotnet-10-upgrade-r1/design.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/azure-deployment.md</file>
    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="list-runtimes" location="projects/dotnet-10-upgrade-r1/design.md">design §7 — verify prod region with `az webapp list-runtimes --os-type linux` (colon form).</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="prescriptive">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Load spec FR-15 + design §7 Unresolved Questions. Declare RIGOR: STANDARD. Confirm operator + Azure auth.</step>
    <step order="1">Run `az webapp list-runtimes --os-type linux`; capture the output; confirm `DOTNETCORE:10.0` present.</step>
    <step order="2">Confirm a staging slot exists (or verify the clean creation path with the operator) on the target App Service.</step>
    <step order="3">Write `notes/region-slot-evidence.md` with the pasted evidence; mark the two Unresolved Questions resolved.</step>
    <step order="4">Update `tasks/TASK-INDEX.md`: set 050 status to ✅.</step>
    <step order="5">Document any deviation in `projects/dotnet-10-upgrade-r1/notes/`.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If `DOTNETCORE:10.0` is NOT available in the prod region, STOP and surface per CLAUDE.md §6 — do NOT reach for a self-contained-publish escape hatch (spec MUST NOT); this is a go/no-go input for the whole cutover.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <tools>
    <tool name="dotnet">n/a (az CLI)</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="doc">projects/dotnet-10-upgrade-r1/notes/region-slot-evidence.md</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">`notes/region-slot-evidence.md` contains real `az webapp list-runtimes` output confirming `DOTNETCORE:10.0` in the prod region.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A staging slot is confirmed to exist or a clean creation path is verified.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: if the runtime is absent in-region, the task STOPPED and escalated (no self-contained workaround).</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>spec FR-15 (evidence half). OPERATOR-DRIVEN. Resolves the two Unresolved Questions in spec.</notes>

  <execution>
    <skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill>
  </execution>
</task>
